WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.067 --> 00:00:18.272
The next three weeks at Green Gables were busy as Anne got ready to go to Queen's College.

2
00:00:18.273 --> 00:00:20.938
Anne had many lovely clothes to take.

3
00:00:20.939 --> 00:00:25.446
It was Matthew who bought Anne's clothes, and Marilla no longer objected.

4
00:00:25.447 --> 00:00:32.277
Anne put on her new green silk dress, and recited a poem for Matthew and Marilla in the kitchen.

5
00:00:32.278 --> 00:00:39.096
Marilla watched Anne's bright, animated face and graceful movements. A tear came to Marilla's eye.

6
00:00:39.097 --> 00:00:44.385
"My poem made you cry, Marilla!" Anne exclaimed.

7
00:00:44.386 --> 00:00:48.474
"No, I wasn't crying over that," Marilla sniffed.

8
00:00:48.475 --> 00:00:51.961
"I was thinking of the little girl you used to be, Anne.

9
00:00:51.962 --> 00:00:58.311
I wish you had stayed a little girl. You've grown up now, and you're going away to college.

10
00:00:58.312 --> 00:01:04.713
You look so tall and stylish and so . . . so different in that dress.

11
00:01:04.714 --> 00:01:07.981
I just get lonely thinking about it."

12
00:01:07.982 --> 00:01:13.287
"Marilla!" Anne took Marilla's hands and looked tenderly into Marilla's eyes.

13
00:01:13.288 --> 00:01:20.120
"I haven't changed, not really. The real me—back here—is just the same.

14
00:01:20.121 --> 00:01:27.440
I will always be your little Anne, who will love you and Matthew and dear Green Gables every day of her life."

15
00:01:27.441 --> 00:01:35.025
Matthew listened, and with suspicious moisture in his eyes, he got up and went outside.

16
00:01:35.026 --> 00:01:39.952
"Well now, I guess she hasn't been spoiled," Matthew said to himself proudly.

17
00:01:39.953 --> 00:01:43.544
"I guess interfering sometimes never did any harm either.

18
00:01:43.545 --> 00:01:48.001
She's smart, pretty, and loving too. She's been a blessing to us.

19
00:01:48.002 --> 00:01:50.823
It was a lucky mistake that Mrs. Spencer made.

20
00:01:50.824 --> 00:01:53.128
But . . . I don't believe it was luck.

21
00:01:53.129 --> 00:01:57.444
No, I believe Anne was sent as a gift from heaven because we needed her."

22
00:01:57.445 --> 00:02:00.202
The day came for Anne to go to college.

23
00:02:00.203 --> 00:02:05.681
After many tearful good-byes, Anne's life as a college student began.

24
00:02:05.682 --> 00:02:10.261
On the first day at Queen's, students met each other and their professors.

25
00:02:10.262 --> 00:02:14.049
Afterwards Anne left the college and went to her boarding house.

26
00:02:14.050 --> 00:02:19.165
She looked dismally at her little room, with its picture-less walls and empty bookcase.

27
00:02:19.166 --> 00:02:22.833
A tear came into her eye as she thought of Green Gables.

28
00:02:22.834 --> 00:02:29.956
Anne started to cry. And a flood of tears would have come if Josie Pye had not appeared at Anne's door.

29
00:02:29.957 --> 00:02:36.729
In the joy of seeing a familiar face, Anne forgot that she and Josie were not good friends, to say the least.

30
00:02:36.730 --> 00:02:40.008
"I'm glad you came," Anne said sincerely.

31
00:02:40.009 --> 00:02:46.662
"You've been crying," Josie remarked. "I suppose you're homesick. Some people have no self-control.

32
00:02:46.663 --> 00:02:51.224
You really shouldn't cry because your nose and eyes get red, and then you seem red all over."

33
00:02:51.225 --> 00:02:55.579
With that, Josie left. Anne scowled and cried again.

34
00:02:55.580 --> 00:03:01.566
Soon Anne's homesickness subsided. She threw herself into her studies and made new friends.

35
00:03:01.567 --> 00:03:04.423
She decided to try for the academic awards:

36
00:03:04.424 --> 00:03:11.213
the gold medal for the best student in general and a scholarship to Redmond University for the best student in English.

37
00:03:11.214 --> 00:03:15.291
"I'll win that scholarship if hard work can do it," she thought.

38
00:03:15.292 --> 00:03:18.783
"Wouldn't Matthew be proud if I got a BA?"

39
00:03:18.784 --> 00:03:23.011
After the Christmas holidays, the students settled down to hard work.

40
00:03:23.012 --> 00:03:30.881
By this time the medal contestants were narrowed down to three: Gilbert Blythe, Anne Shirley, and Lewis Wilson.

41
00:03:30.882 --> 00:03:35.852
The scholarship was more doubtful, with any one of six students being a possible winner.

42
00:03:35.853 --> 00:03:42.933
Anne's rivalry with Gilbert was as intense as ever, but for some reason the bitterness had gone out of it.

43
00:03:42.934 --> 00:03:47.123
Spring came, but at Queen's there was talk only of exams.

44
00:03:47.124 --> 00:03:50.772
"Ruby, sometimes I feel like exams mean everything.

45
00:03:50.773 --> 00:03:56.855
But when I look at the flowers blossoming, the exams don't seem as important," said Anne.

46
00:03:56.856 --> 00:03:59.187
Ruby Gillis did not share this view.

47
00:03:59.188 --> 00:04:04.276
To her, exams were very important, far more important than flowers!

48
00:04:04.277 --> 00:04:10.350
Besides, Anne was sure to pass all her exams while Ruby was not so certain.

49
00:04:10.351 --> 00:04:15.472
It was the morning the exam results were to be posted on the notice board at Queen's College.

50
00:04:15.473 --> 00:04:18.648
Anne and Jane Andrews walked down the street together.

51
00:04:18.649 --> 00:04:23.695
Jane was smiling and happy; exams were over and she had passed at least.

52
00:04:23.696 --> 00:04:31.276
Anne was pale and quiet. In ten minutes she would know who had won the medal and the scholarship.

53
00:04:31.277 --> 00:04:35.713
"I don't have the courage to march up to that notice board, Jane," Anne said.

54
00:04:35.714 --> 00:04:40.394
"You must read it and tell me. And try to do it as quickly as possible.

55
00:04:40.395 --> 00:04:47.785
If I failed, just tell me, and whatever you do, don't try to sympathize with me. Promise me, Jane."

56
00:04:47.786 --> 00:04:53.004
Jane promised solemnly, but as it happened, there was no need for such a promise.

57
00:04:53.005 --> 00:05:01.612
Anne and Jane found a group of boys carrying Gilbert Blythe on their shoulders and yelling, "Hooray for Gilbert, medalist!"

58
00:05:01.613 --> 00:05:06.797
Anne felt a pang of defeat and disappointment. So Gilbert had won.

59
00:05:06.798 --> 00:05:11.605
Well, Matthew would be sorry. He had been so sure she would win.

60
00:05:11.606 --> 00:05:17.796
And then somebody called out, "Three cheers for Anne Shirley, winner of the scholarship!"

61
00:05:17.797 --> 00:05:24.955
Suddenly many students were around them, and Anne was the center of a laughing, congratulating group.

62
00:05:24.956 --> 00:05:34.673
She was pushed and pulled and hugged, but she managed to whisper to Jane, "Oh, won't Matthew and Marilla be pleased? I must write home right away."

63
00:05:34.674 --> 00:05:40.492
After the scholarship and medal ceremony, Anne went home to Avonlea with Matthew and Marilla.

64
00:05:40.493 --> 00:05:43.266
Diana was at Green Gables to greet her.

65
00:05:43.267 --> 00:05:49.044
"It's so good to be home again," cried Anne, "and it's good to see you.

66
00:05:49.045 --> 00:05:51.425
I have so many things to tell you.

67
00:05:51.426 --> 00:05:55.583
But now I'm tired—tired of being studious.

68
00:05:55.584 --> 00:06:01.522
I'll spend two hours tomorrow lying on the grass, thinking of absolutely nothing."

69
00:06:01.523 --> 00:06:04.661
"You've done so well, Anne," said Diana.

70
00:06:04.662 --> 00:06:08.731
"I suppose you won't be teaching, now that you've won the scholarship?"

71
00:06:08.732 --> 00:06:15.132
"No, I won't," said Anne. "I'll go to the Redmond University in September."

72
00:06:15.133 --> 00:06:21.690
"Jane's going to teach in Newbridge," said Diana, "and Gilbert is going to teach too. He must.

73
00:06:21.691 --> 00:06:28.109
His father can't afford to send him to college next year, so he will work instead and save up the money for it."

74
00:06:28.110 --> 00:06:33.964
Anne felt a little dismayed. She had expected Gilbert to go to Redmond University as well.

75
00:06:33.965 --> 00:06:37.186
What would she do without their rivalry to inspire her?

76
00:06:37.187 --> 00:06:49.588
And what would she do without her friends from Avonlea?
